{"text":"MODEL_FEEDBACK_JSON:
{
  "positive_alignment_reasons": [
    "The small bags feel like a natural next purchase because my screws, nuts, and rivets need to stay separated and easy to find; the pegboards could similarly help keep my growing tool collection accessible if they can support it.",
    "The gap-filling glue fits my repair work because it could handle small repairs where my adhesive tapes are unsuitable. It adds a useful capability alongside supplies I already have."
  ],
  "negative_misalignment_reasons": [
    "Both printer filaments and the breadboards assume projects I have not shown a need for. My recent tools and supplies support mechanical repairs and fabrication, without establishing that I print parts or prototype electronics.",
    "The calibration weights do not serve my recent dimensional and temperature measuring needs, and four large trash cans are far beyond the workspace cleanup supplies I currently need.",
    "The infrared thermometer and machine screw kit fit my work, but I recently obtained similar items. Being relevant does not make them useful purchases right now."
  ],
  "overgeneralized_signals": [
    "My interest in hands-on projects seems to have been stretched into an assumed need for almost any workshop or maker supply.",
    "My repeated fastener purchases and recent thermometer purchase seem to have been treated as reasons to buy more similar products without enough attention to what I already have."
  ],
  "missing_or_underweighted_signals": [
    "My growing collection of hardware creates a practical need for sorting and storage, which makes small bags especially useful now.",
    "I care about whether an item fills a remaining repair need, duplicates existing supplies, or requires equipment and projects I have not mentioned.",
    "Quantity and suitability matter: I could use modest tool organization, subject to load capacity, but do not need four large garbage cans."
  ],
  "summary_diagnosis": "The recommendations recognize my repair and fastening work, but sometimes confuse related workshop supplies with things I currently need."
}"}
